WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.958 --> 00:00:31.625
<b>In the previous two verses,</b>

2
00:00:31.625 --> 00:00:36.458
<b>Lord Krishna described the foolish person</b>

3
00:00:36.458 --> 00:00:41.708
<b>who is absorbed in material attachments</b>
<b>and performs only self-interested actions.</b>

4
00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:46.708
<b>He also explained the nature of the wise,</b>

5
00:00:46.708 --> 00:00:51.708
<b>who unaffected by materialism, </b>
<b>perform selfless actions.</b>

6
00:00:51.708 --> 00:00:52.500
<b>But</b>

7
00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:00.791
<b>what should a wise person do when they </b>
<b>encounter someone trapped in ignorance?</b>

8
00:01:00.791 --> 00:01:04.166
<b>Should they try to change the ignorant person?</b>

9
00:01:04.166 --> 00:01:09.375
<b>Should they influence them to renounce material</b>
<b>pleasures by imparting knowledge?</b>

10
00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:13.250
<b>And what if they don't - would that be right?</b>

11
00:01:13.250 --> 00:01:18.041
<b>In this verse, Lord Krishna </b>
<b>addresses this very dilemma.</b>

12
00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:25.583
<b>Lord Krishna in this verse says,</b>

13
00:01:25.583 --> 00:01:31.541
<b>that people deluded by material nature </b>
<b>remain attached to the fruits of their actions –</b>

14
00:01:31.541 --> 00:01:33.458
<b>such a person is ignorant.</b>

15
00:01:33.458 --> 00:01:39.083
<b>However, those who possess true </b>
<b>wisdom should not disturb such ignorant ones.</b>

16
00:01:39.083 --> 00:01:42.541
<b>Now, you might wonder:</b>

17
00:01:42.541 --> 00:01:45.041
<b>when you encounter an ignorant person</b>

18
00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:49.625
<b>what's wrong with illuminating their</b>
<b>minds with complete knowledge?</b>

19
00:01:49.625 --> 00:01:55.041
<b>What's wrong with inspiring them to abandon </b>
<b> their attachment to material pleasures?</b>

20
00:01:55.041 --> 00:01:56.583
<b>This question is natural</b>

21
00:01:56.583 --> 00:02:00.958
<b>and to answer it, we must understand </b>
<b>the deeper meaning of this verse.</b>

22
00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:02.125
<b>Consider this:</b>

23
00:02:02.125 --> 00:02:04.791
<b>if someone loves sweets</b>

24
00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:09.958
<b>and can't finish a meal without having dessert,</b>

25
00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:12.125
<b>what happens when a well-wisher</b>

26
00:02:12.125 --> 00:02:19.333
<b>starts listing the harmful effects of </b>
<b>sugar and pressures them to give up sweets?</b>

27
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:24.208
<b>Most likely, that person won't give up sweets</b>

28
00:02:24.208 --> 00:02:28.791
<b>but will become disturbed by</b>
<b>this well-intentioned advice.</b>

29
00:02:28.791 --> 00:02:34.375
<b>They might even stop discussing the </b>
<b>topic with their well-wisher altogether.</b>

30
00:02:34.375 --> 00:02:36.541
<b>This is the nature of attachment –</b>

31
00:02:36.541 --> 00:02:41.208
<b>when a person cannot comprehend </b>
<b>even what's good for them.</b>

32
00:02:41.208 --> 00:02:43.625
<b>Now ask yourself:</b>

33
00:02:43.625 --> 00:02:45.083
<b>what would be better?</b>

34
00:02:45.083 --> 00:02:48.708
<b>Trying to explain complete knowledge verbally,</b>

35
00:02:48.708 --> 00:02:56.208
<b>or becoming an example yourself and </b>
<b>gradually inspiring others over time?</b>

36
00:02:56.208 --> 00:03:01.791
<b>If you fill an unbaked pot with too much water,</b>

37
00:03:01.791 --> 00:03:05.750
<b>both the pot will break and the water will spill.</b>

38
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.708
<b>Not only will there be immediate damage,</b>

39
00:03:07.708 --> 00:03:13.125
<b>but the possibility of storing water </b>
<b>in the future will also be lost.</b>

40
00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:14.166
<b>Similarly,</b>

41
00:03:14.166 --> 00:03:16.708
<b>before acquiring deep knowledge,</b>

42
00:03:16.708 --> 00:03:20.708
<b>it's essential for a person's mind to mature.</b>

43
00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:23.333
<b>A truly wise person understands this.</b>

44
00:03:23.333 --> 00:03:28.416
<b>This is why they don't disturb the </b>
<b>ignorant with the influence of their knowledge.</b>

45
00:03:28.416 --> 00:03:31.250
<b>Instead, they set an example</b>

46
00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:39.875
<b>and make subtle efforts to inspire those who come </b>
<b>into their contact as time brings maturity.</b>

47
00:03:39.875 --> 00:03:42.375
<b>Their goal is others' improvement,</b>

48
00:03:42.375 --> 00:03:44.375
<b>and therefore it's appropriate</b>

49
00:03:44.375 --> 00:03:49.125
<b>to communicate with others according </b>
<b>to their level of understanding.</b>

50
00:03:49.125 --> 00:03:52.041
<b>Improvement requires not just knowledge,</b>

51
00:03:52.041 --> 00:03:55.916
<b>but also the right maturity and time.</b>

52
00:03:55.916 --> 00:03:58.708
<b>This is what we must understand.</b>

53
00:04:03.458 --> 00:04:07.166
<b>In our daily lives, we meet many people</b>

54
00:04:07.166 --> 00:04:13.083
<b>who are at different stages of their </b>
<b>spiritual and personal growth.</b>

55
00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:18.625
<b>If we try to offer the same kind of help to everyone,</b>

56
00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:24.000
<b>it won't benefit most people.</b>

57
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:26.291
<b>Think of it this way:</b>

58
00:04:26.291 --> 00:04:31.000
<b>Imagine you're skilled in mathematics,</b>

59
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:37.333
<b>and you need to help a friend or younger sibling.</b>

60
00:04:37.333 --> 00:04:39.083
<b>What would be the right approach?</b>

61
00:04:39.083 --> 00:04:45.333
<b>Would it be wise to start with complex </b>
<b>problems based on your advanced knowledge?</b>

62
00:04:45.333 --> 00:04:47.916
<b>Or would it be better</b>

63
00:04:47.916 --> 00:04:54.333
<b>to begin with simple formulas suited </b>
<b>to their level and needs,</b>

64
00:04:54.333 --> 00:05:00.166
<b>then gradually progress to </b>
<b>more complex concepts?</b>

65
00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.958
<b>Whether in education or life,</b>

66
00:05:02.958 --> 00:05:06.625
<b>the fundamental principle of </b>
<b>guidance remains the same –</b>

67
00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:12.083
<b>it must be tailored to the person being helped.</b>

68
00:05:12.083 --> 00:05:16.833
<b>For this, remember these four essential principles:</b>

69
00:05:16.833 --> 00:05:17.875
<b>First -</b>

70
00:05:17.875 --> 00:05:23.583
<b>Understand the level of </b>
<b>the person you wish to help</b>

71
00:05:23.583 --> 00:05:24.875
<b>Second -</b>

72
00:05:24.875 --> 00:05:29.208
<b>Begin with simple teachings </b>
<b>according to their level;</b>

73
00:05:29.208 --> 00:05:31.666
<b>this will encourage them</b>

74
00:05:31.666 --> 00:05:32.583
<b>Third -</b>

75
00:05:32.583 --> 00:05:35.916
<b>Continuously assess their progress.</b>

76
00:05:35.916 --> 00:05:40.875
<b>This can be done by setting small goals,</b>

77
00:05:40.875 --> 00:05:45.958
<b>helping you determine when to </b>
<b>increase the level of support</b>

78
00:05:45.958 --> 00:05:49.791
<b>Fourth and most important -</b>

79
00:05:49.791 --> 00:05:55.208
<b>Maintain gentleness throughout this process –</b>

80
00:05:55.208 --> 00:05:56.625
<b>remember,</b>

81
00:05:56.625 --> 00:06:00.000
<b>your purpose is to help others,</b>

82
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:09.458
<b>not to show off or demonstrate how wise </b>
<b>and knowledgeable you are.</b>

83
00:06:09.458 --> 00:06:14.416
<b>If you help others in this way,</b>

84
00:06:14.416 --> 00:06:18.083
<b>you'll naturally earn their respect and affection.</b>

85
00:06:18.083 --> 00:06:21.000
<b>Moreover, you'll discover</b>

86
00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:27.750
<b>the joy of selflessly contributing </b>
<b>to someone else's growth.</b>

87
00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:33.791
<b>This too is a form of selfless action.</b>

88
00:06:33.791 --> 00:06:35.750
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

89
00:06:40.375 --> 00:06:44.875
<b>In social and family settings, </b>
<b>we often encounter people</b>

90
00:06:44.875 --> 00:06:52.416
<b>whose spiritual thoughts and level </b>
<b>of understanding differ from our own.</b>

91
00:06:52.416 --> 00:07:00.125
<b>This verse teaches us how</b>
<b>to handle such differences.</b>

92
00:07:00.125 --> 00:07:07.458
<b>It instructs that when others' spiritual </b>
<b>progress or understanding differs from yours,</b>

93
00:07:07.458 --> 00:07:12.083
<b>you should respond with </b>
<b>patience and gentleness.</b>

94
00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:16.916
<b>Consider a family gathering</b>

95
00:07:16.916 --> 00:07:23.250
<b>where everyone has different perspectives </b>
<b>and understandings of life.</b>

96
00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:30.041
<b>It's like a garden with plants of various colors.</b>

97
00:07:30.041 --> 00:07:34.375
<b>Does every plant need the</b>
<b>same amount of sunlight?</b>

98
00:07:34.375 --> 00:07:35.375
<b>No.</b>

99
00:07:35.375 --> 00:07:39.333
<b>Does every plant need the same amount </b>
<b>of fertilizer and water?</b>

100
00:07:39.333 --> 00:07:40.416
<b>No.</b>

101
00:07:40.416 --> 00:07:43.333
<b>A skilled gardener knows</b>

102
00:07:43.333 --> 00:07:46.458
<b>that each plant has its own level,</b>

103
00:07:46.458 --> 00:07:49.666
<b>its own care requirements.</b>

104
00:07:49.666 --> 00:07:54.875
<b>Placing all plants in direct </b>
<b>sunlight wouldn't be right.</b>

105
00:07:54.875 --> 00:08:00.208
<b>Giving excessive water to all would be harmful.</b>

106
00:08:00.208 --> 00:08:06.916
<b>We must adopt this gardener's mindset </b>
<b>in our family and social environment.</b>

107
00:08:06.916 --> 00:08:13.791
<b>Understanding everyone with gentleness </b>
<b>and communicating accordingly.</b>

108
00:08:13.791 --> 00:08:15.166
<b>Think about it –</b>

109
00:08:15.166 --> 00:08:20.958
<b>if someone in your family is absorbed </b>
<b>in material pleasures,</b>

110
00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:24.750
<b>and you try to force your wisdom upon them,</b>

111
00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.958
<b>claiming their way of life is wrong,</b>

112
00:08:27.958 --> 00:08:34.333
<b>they might become hostile rather than change.</b>

113
00:08:34.333 --> 00:08:38.541
<b>Could you help them then?</b>

114
00:08:38.541 --> 00:08:40.291
<b>No.</b>

115
00:08:40.291 --> 00:08:42.458
<b>So what should be done?</b>

116
00:08:42.458 --> 00:08:48.333
<b>Instead of commenting on others' lifestyles,</b>

117
00:08:48.333 --> 00:08:56.708
<b>share stories from your own life where </b>
<b>spirituality and life lessons helped you.</b>

118
00:08:56.708 --> 00:09:01.375
<b>This becomes an indirect way of inspiring others.</b>

119
00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:05.041
<b>If someone asks questions about this,</b>

120
00:09:05.041 --> 00:09:11.041
<b>it indicates their willingness </b>
<b>to learn and understand.</b>

121
00:09:11.041 --> 00:09:16.750
<b>In such situations, you can explain </b>
<b>the depth of your thoughts.</b>

122
00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:17.833
<b>However,</b>

123
00:09:17.833 --> 00:09:20.458
<b>if someone shows no interest,</b>

124
00:09:20.458 --> 00:09:25.125
<b>it's a sign not to disturb them.</b>

125
00:09:25.125 --> 00:09:27.666
<b>This verse teaches us</b>

126
00:09:27.666 --> 00:09:30.666
<b>to respect everyone's level</b>

127
00:09:30.666 --> 00:09:36.291
<b>and to help others with patience.</b>

128
00:09:40.958 --> 00:09:48.375
<b>In our professional life, our workplace is </b>
<b>also like a garden –</b>

129
00:09:48.375 --> 00:09:50.875
<b>with different plants,</b>

130
00:09:50.875 --> 00:09:58.166
<b>each with its own color, growth rate, </b>
<b>uniqueness, and significance.</b>

131
00:09:58.166 --> 00:10:03.208
<b>If you lead some colleagues,</b>

132
00:10:03.208 --> 00:10:07.875
<b>consider yourself the gardener of this garden.</b>

133
00:10:07.875 --> 00:10:11.625
<b>How would a gardener nurture this garden?</b>

134
00:10:11.625 --> 00:10:19.375
<b>Would they give the same amount of</b>
<b>water to a small new plant as to a large tree?</b>

135
00:10:19.375 --> 00:10:20.833
<b>No,</b>

136
00:10:20.833 --> 00:10:26.625
<b>they would give less to the small plant</b>
<b>and more to the large tree.</b>

137
00:10:26.625 --> 00:10:34.291
<b>Would they try to make a plant </b>
<b>that normally takes months to flower,</b>

138
00:10:34.291 --> 00:10:37.750
<b>bloom in just days or hours?</b>

139
00:10:37.750 --> 00:10:39.375
<b>No,</b>

140
00:10:39.375 --> 00:10:44.125
<b>they would remain patient </b>
<b>and wait for the right time.</b>

141
00:10:44.125 --> 00:10:49.333
<b>Now apply these principles to the workplace.</b>

142
00:10:49.333 --> 00:10:58.125
<b>Is it right to pressure a new colleague</b>
<b>beyond their pace and capability?</b>

143
00:10:58.125 --> 00:11:04.458
<b>Or is it better to teach them gradually?</b>

144
00:11:04.458 --> 00:11:09.666
<b>As an experienced person, </b>
<b>who needs your experience more?</b>

145
00:11:09.666 --> 00:11:15.625
<b>Those who are mature, or those who aren't?</b>

146
00:11:15.625 --> 00:11:16.916
<b>Moreover,</b>

147
00:11:16.916 --> 00:11:20.791
<b>would a gardener become disturbed</b>

148
00:11:20.791 --> 00:11:26.291
<b>thinking why some plants produce fewer </b>
<b>flowers while others produce more?</b>

149
00:11:26.291 --> 00:11:27.500
<b>No...</b>

150
00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:29.750
<b>they won't be disturbed</b>

151
00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:32.708
<b>because this is nature's law –</b>

152
00:11:32.708 --> 00:11:36.708
<b>each has its own yield.</b>

153
00:11:36.708 --> 00:11:38.541
<b>Similarly,</b>

154
00:11:38.541 --> 00:11:44.083
<b>a person in a leadership position</b>
<b>at work must understand</b>

155
00:11:44.083 --> 00:11:46.625
<b>that everyone has different capabilities.</b>

156
00:11:46.625 --> 00:11:53.541
<b>They must patiently support people according </b>
<b>to their abilities without getting disturbed.</b>

157
00:11:53.541 --> 00:11:58.375
<b>And if someone makes an unintentional mistake,</b>

158
00:11:58.375 --> 00:12:06.291
<b>true leadership is identified by </b>
<b>handling the situation with gentleness.</b>

159
00:12:06.291 --> 00:12:11.250
<b>Teach the person who made the mistake calmly.</b>

160
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.166
<b>Remember,</b>

161
00:12:13.166 --> 00:12:17.833
<b>your goal is to help them improve,</b>

162
00:12:17.833 --> 00:12:25.125
<b>not to humiliate them.</b>
<b>Reflect on all these points.</b>

163
00:12:25.125 --> 00:12:31.500
<b>They are extremely important for professional life.</b>

